imum flexibility with my T2, T2, T3, T3, T4 tiles (which can form multiple chow combinations) and preserve the B7, B8, B9 sequence along with the J1, J1, J1 pung. This keeps my hand moving toward a valid winning pattern with sufficient points.\n\nAnswer: Play W6"}
